\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 EXECUTIVE SUMMARY The objective is to update the Photobooth iPad application to support a "Burst Mode / Animated GIF" workflow. Users will be able to create looping GIFs in addition to standard photos. This requires updates to the Settings, Home Screen UI, Camera Logic, and Sharing workflows.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CONFIGURATION & SETTINGS New settings must be clustered under a section titled "Animated GIF", positioned immediately after the "Timers and Counts" block.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Master Toggle: "Enable Animated GIF Mode" (Boolean, Default: Off). Controls Home Screen layout.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Frame Count: "GIF Frame Count" (Integer, Default: 4). Total images to capture for the GIF.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Capture Interval: "GIF Capture Interval" (Float, Default: 0.25s). Delay between burst captures.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Playback Speed: "GIF Frame Duration" (Float, Default: 0.25s). Time per frame in the final GIF.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Resolution: "GIF Resolution" (Enum, Options: 720p, 480p, Default: 720p). Resolution of the GIF frames.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 HOME SCREEN UI/UX Behavior is determined by the "Enable Animated GIF Mode" toggle.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
